\cf0 Sir Issac Newton has been described as the greatest intellect that ever lived, but when he was stumped to mathematically explain all of the interactions of the planets in the solar system, he turned to god as the answer and he stopped his inquiries. It took another 100 years for Laplace to solve the riddle with perturbation theory mathematics. When god is invoked, all progress is halted until someone else comes along and picks up where the others left off. 
